  "contract": {
    "statement": "For recurrent C005 state X_n and its C004 successor slot s_{n+1}=(p,rho,c), M001 defines the unique ordered birth-local cut of the already-born carrier. The boundary is exactly the C005 carrier subsequence consisting of the root-to-parent provenance prefix chain of p together with already-born same-parent siblings of ranks < rho; the interior is the complementary carrier subsequence. The unborn child c is in neither block.",
    "ownership_boundary": [
      "consumes only C005 current born carrier and the C004 next open provenance slot",
      "uses only primitive provenance prefix/parent/sibling-rank roles already fixed by C003/C018/C004",
      "inherits boundary and interior order from the C005/C018 carrier order and introduces no new ordering convention",
      "does not inspect conductance values or response data",
      "does not introduce sampling caps, frontier radii, metric neighborhoods, environment ports or downstream geometry",
      "does not perform Schur/DtN elimination, define the interior-domain theorem M002, compute R_n, create a birth or update X_n"
    ]
  },
  "cross_layer": {
    "equivalence": "Python and Lean define the same ordered partition of the same C005 born carrier by the same provenance predicate: root-to-parent prefix-chain membership or earlier same-parent sibling membership relative to the C004 slot. Python filters state.nodes; Lean filters canonicalCarrier X. Both exclude the unborn C004 child and preserve inherited carrier order.",
    "semantic_mismatch_known": false,
